 ## Overview
-Computational Space Traversal is a method for rendering data on curvilinear (non-uniform) grids by mapping the irregular physical domain to a regular computational space [S1]. It solves the difficulty of resampling scalar values along a ray in distorted geometry by performing the traversal in the regular computational space, where standard incremental grid traversal applies [S1]. Unlike [Uniform Grid Traversal](9652-uniform-grid-traversal.md), which assumes uniform spacing, this method handles arbitrary hexahedral meshes by transforming ray segments and vectors using Jacobian matrices [S1].
+Computational Space Traversal renders data on curvilinear grids by mapping the irregular physical domain to a regular computational space [S1]. It solves the difficulty of resampling scalar values along a ray in distorted geometry by performing the traversal in the regular computational space, where standard incremental grid traversal applies [S1]. Unlike [Uniform Grid Traversal](9652-uniform-grid-traversal.md), which assumes uniform spacing, this method handles arbitrary hexahedral meshes by transforming ray segments and vectors using Jacobian matrices [S1].
 
